  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You call forth an aberrant spirit. It appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range and uses the Aberrant Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose Beholderkin, Mind Flayer, or Slaad. The creature looks like an Aberration of that kind, which determines some details of its stat block. It disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends.</p><p>The creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn immediately after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required by you); if you give none, it takes the Dodge action and uses its movement to avoid danger.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> Use the spell slot’s level for the spell’s level in the stat block.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-yXTyrCOlrngnGnMf\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Summon asks for the kind. The spirit’s AC, Hit Points and attack damage include the spell’s level, and Whispering Aura uses your spell save DC.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
